Description: Reconstructs age-specific survivorship profiles under a stable and
 stationary population assumption using a Weibull survival model. Given an
 age-specific fertility schedule, the package generates Weibull profiles that
 satisfy the demographic constraint R0 = sum(lx * mx) = 1, scans candidate beta
 values, optionally selects the constrained profile that best reproduces an
 observed survivorship schedule, and derives stable age structures and mortality
 profiles. It also provides a free two-parameter Weibull fit as a descriptive
 reference and separate Excel workflows for the historical and extended routes.
 Methods are based on Martín-González et al. (2019)
 <doi:10.1016/j.jasrep.2019.03.031>.
